{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDE2L0NpdHklMjBPZiUyMEpveSUyMCUyODIwMTYlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"City Of Joy","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/pQwjmlxCPYyUyh4DpJpfDgxFyC9.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ylUBY5u08TUt4mSYNW30Sw9wK8D.jpg","description":"The Democratic Republic of Congo has endured 20 years of devastating violence. Rape has been used as a weapon of war to destroy community and access precious minerals. Congo is often referred to as “the worst place in the world to be a woman.” \"City of Joy\" tells a different story of the region. The film focuses on Jane, a student at a center where women who have suffered unimaginable abuse join together to become leaders. We also meet the founders of the center: a devout Congolese Doctor, a Congolese activist, and a radical N.Y. playwright. The film weaves between joy and pain as these individuals band together to demand hope in a place so often deemed hopeless.\n\nReleased 11 Nov 2016 · Congo, United States of America · Language: English · 74 min\nStudio: Essence Road, Impact Partners\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2016","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.3","runtime":"74 min","cast":["Christine Schuler-Deschryver","Denis Mukwege Mukengere","V","Jane Mukunilwa"],"director":["Madeleine Gavin"],"released":"2016-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"When we tell the truth, we change the world","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Madeleine Gavin","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/A9FsDNrrLSeXd5HSHees3codK5H.jpg"},{"name":"Christine Schuler-Deschryver","character":"Herself"},{"name":"Denis Mukwege Mukengere","character":"Himself","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/xRPnxslR1iNVoURiE2t99PfX8E6.jpg"},{"name":"V","character":"Herself","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/utzboZ5Pzl9I44Z7ZKKiOQYn3Lc.jpg"},{"name":"Jane Mukunilwa","character":"Herself"}]},"trailers":[{"source":"MNy